Step 1 — Open your project folder
Run these commands in your Linux terminal:
cd ~/cicd-demo
ls


Make sure Main.java is present. The filename must match the capital M.
Step 2 — Create the Dockerfile
Run:
nano Dockerfile


Paste this code:

FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jdk

WORKDIR /app

COPY Main.java .

RUN javac Main.java

CMD ["java", "Main"]



Save the file using Ctrl + O, press Enter, and exit with Ctrl + X.
Step 3 — Build the Docker image
Run:
docker build -t cicd-java-app:1.0 .


Docker will download the Java 17 base image if needed, compile your program, and create the image.
Step 4 — Run the container
docker run --rm cicd-java-app:1.0


Expected output:
CI/CD Pipeline using Java is working successfully!


Step 5 — Verify the image
docker images


You should see cicd-java-app in the image list.
